    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Res-Carrefour-Sherb/Protection-Supervisor_JR0000070006": {
      "title": "Protection Supervisor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Student Housing & Hospitality Services Position Summary: Reporting to the Associate Director Protection, Student Housing & Hospitality Services, the Protection Supervisor is responsible for the day-to-day operations by directing a team of Night Stewards within the Unit. Provides the best possible direction of comprehensive programs related to security services, emergency preparedness, fire prevention and environmental health and safety in an environment that fosters a sense of community, enhances student learning/safety and supports the overall mission of the SHHS unit within the University. Fosters a safe and healthy environment for students, staff and visitors while enforcing policies, procedures, legislation and regulations concerning building access control, thefts and incidents, accidents and safety training. Primary Responsibilities: Directly supervise the team of approximately 10 to 20 Night Stewards and casuals, including participating in the hiring, interviewing. Make recommendations on probation or bring up issues to the Associate Director Protection. Train and coach staff and organize activities to support the day/night operations of the unit by ensuring that functions are carried out in accordance with established goals and objectives. Implement administrative procedures in support of the unit's operation. Assist with the organization of security , fire protection, safety, environmental and occupational health programs, are adminsitered in conformity with established procedures and guidelines. Participate in public awareness activities by promoting the services offered. . Plan and oversee the implementation of projects. Participate in the writing of documents or reports related to issues (e.g. security, emergency measure, fire prevention, environmental health and safety, access control, etc.). Administer safety inspections of the unit's buildings, as per legislation and regulations. When appropriate, inform the Associate Director Protection of discrepancies and formulate recommendations. Provide support /resources/assistance to the communities for security and /or safety concerns. Provide assistance and liaise with University Safety office related to queries from internals and externals. Support emergency response operations and emergency preparedness program protocol; and respond to incidents in accordance with response procedures and communicated directives. Establish the work schedule on a rotational basis. Ensure back-up list is available in case of Night Steward vacation or unplanned leave. Establish and foster effective working relationships by identifying needs and providing support in the delivery of services. Produces quarterly reports/monthly evaluations and presents it to the Associate Director Protection for review. Assist employees in their training. Conducts rounds/patrols(overnight) within the SHHS, including Solin Hall. Strong knowledge of Collective Union Agreements. Minimum Education & Experience: DEC III Three (3) years' related experience Other Qualifying Skills And/Or Abilities: Required: Security Permit (BSP) and First Aid. Experience in the support, training and supervision of staff. Experience in a security environment, particularly working in a university student residence operation. Demonstrated ability to supervise unionized staff as well as able to interpret collective agreements. Proven organizational and leadership skills along with excellent interpersonal, communication and problem-solving skills. Ability to work as part of a team. Proven ability to adapt to flexible year round schedules. Excellent written and verbal communication skills in French and English. Additional Information: This is an overnight position (Sunday, Monday, Thursday, Friday & Saturday 21h00 to 5h00, may be subject to change). Knowledge of French and English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level 4 on a scale of 0-4. Minimum Education and Experience: DEC III 3 Years Related Experience / Annual Salary: (MPEX Grade 03) $63,350.00 - $74,530.00 - $85,710.00 Job Profile: MPEX-LOG1B - Security, Safety & Environment - Professional 1 (Excluded) Hours per Week: 33.75 (Full time) Sunday, Monday, Thursday, Friday, Saturday Supervisor: Associate Director Protection Position End Date (If applicable): Deadline to Apply: 2026-09-30 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
