    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/McIntyre--Medical/Administrative-Coordinator_JR0000082381": {
      "title": "Administrative Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). The Administrative Coordinator provides high-level administrative support to the Department Chair and leadership team. This role is responsible for coordinating departmental activities, academic affairs processes, organizing events, and ensuring the smooth operation of the department. The incumbent serves as a key liaison between faculty, staff, students, and external stakeholders while maintaining a high degree of professionalism, discretion, and attention to detail. Major duties and Responsibilities: · Provide direct administrative support to the Department Chair · Schedule and coordinate departmental activities and meetings, prepare agenda, meeting material, take minutes · Draft and edit correspondence, reports, departmental communications, and official documents. · Provide administrative support with special projects and initiatives as assigned by departmental leadership. · Coordinate departmental and faculty committees that occur throughout the year. · Prepare meeting agendas and supporting materials. · Record and distribute meeting minutes and monitor follow-up action items. · Maintain committee records and ensure completion of required documentation and approvals. · Develop PowerPoint presentations and supporting materials for committee and departmental meetings. · Coordinate and track academic appointments, reappointments, renewals, and administrative appointments. · Support the recruitment and onboarding of visiting professors, including travel and accommodation arrangements. · Assist with departmental advertising, faculty promotions, retirements, and recognition initiatives. · Maintain records and monitor key academic deadlines and processes. · Prepare recommendation letters, reference letters, award nominations, and supporting documentation. · Process purchase orders, assist with expense reports when needed · Assist with financial tracking. · Coordinate sponsorship agreements and donation-related activities. · Prepare and reconcile expenses in accordance with institutional policies. · Liaise with finance and procurement units to ensure timely processing of transactions. · Plan and coordinate departmental and faculty events from conception to completion such as retreats, recognition events, and special celebrations. · Prepare promotional materials with the communications team and communicate the related to events. · Maintain and update departmental website content to ensure accuracy and relevance. The list of duties and responsibilities outlined above is representative and not a complete and detailed list of tasks which may be performed by an employee whose position has been matched to this generic job description. Other Qualifying Skills and/or Abilities: Must be able to prioritize multiple requests, including the ability to conduct comprehensive evaluation of issues to determine priorities. Must be able to demonstrate a high level of professionalism and discretion at all times. Experience with planning meetings and events. Ability to work both independently and as a team play Proven flexibility in order to adapt to tight deadlines, frequent changes and demands. Meticulous in documenting follow-up actions regarding ongoing files. Proven ability to work with computer applications, and Microsoft Office applications such as Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook, teams, SharePoint, etc... English and French, spoken and written.  As one of Montreal's Top Employers, here is what we offer: Competitive benefits package (Health, Dental, Life Insurance) (if eligible) Defined contribution pension plan (with employer contribution up to 10%) (if eligible) Group Registered Retirement Savings Plan (RRSP) and Tax Free Savings Account (TFSA) Competitive vacation policy Two (2) personal days Two (2) floating holidays Nine (9) \"Summer Fridays\" - paid days off between the St-Jean Baptiste holiday and Labour Day Paid time off over the December holiday period Tuition waiver for regular employees and their dependents Up to two (2) days of remote work per week where the position permits Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level # 4 on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: DEP - Secretarial Studies 4 Years Related Experience / DEP - Office Systems Hourly Salary: (MUNACA Level F) $29.42 - $36.46 Hours per Week: 33.75 (Full time) Supervisor: Associate Director, Administration Position End Date (If applicable): 2027-11-30 Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-27 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/McGill-College-2001/Clinic-Manager_JR0000080867": {
      "title": "Clinic Manager",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nFull time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Position Summary: Reporting to the Associate Director Administration, the Clinic Manager is responsible for managing all operations of the Undergraduate Teaching Clinic of the Faculty of Dental Medicine and Oral Health Sciences, in support of the Faculty’s undergraduate teaching program (DMD). This includes planning, development and implementation of all administrative processes and supporting policies for the unit; development of standards, practices and systems and acting as a liaison with other University units, Finance and external organizations. The Clinic Manager provides leadership, professional advice and guidance as well as administrative support to the Associate Dean, Clinical Affairs, and supervises clinical staff including Administrators, Receptionists, Dental Assistants. Develops, implements and monitors electronic filing and document sharing systems. Ensures comprehensive, integrated record keeping, proper management of contracts, and timely follow-ups of all service agreements and other formal relationships. Primary Responsibilities: Manages the day-to-day operations and financial transactions of the Undergraduate Teaching Clinic. Supervises, leads and coaches all staff of the Undergraduate Teaching Clinic, including Administrators, Receptionists, Dental Assistants, and Dispensary Technicians; manages labour related matters in collaboration with the HR Advisor and the Associate Director of Administration ; provides staff development, learning and team-building opportunities. Ensures a healthy work environment and implements equity, diversity and inclusion strategies to increase social sustainability in the Faculty of Dental Medicine and Oral Health Sciences. Promotes effective communication strategies and engages clinical staff in decision-making processes related to their duties to ensure positive relationships in the work environment. Ensures effective budgetary controls for the Undergraduate Teaching Clinic, in collaboration with the Associate Dean, Clinic and the Finance team. Monitors the day-to-day utilization of clinical units; provides regular reports to the Associate Dean, Clinical Affairs and develops strategies to optimize the utilization and productivity of clinical activities. Ensures that University Financial and Procurement policies and procedures are followed. Prepares periodic variance reports for the Finance team. Collaborates with relevant staff on inventory management and stockroom operations, including purchasing activities for the Undergraduate Teaching Clinic, in collaboration with the Finance team. Ensures that the Undergraduate Teaching Clinic meets the standards of the Ordre des dentistes du Québec (ODQ) . In close collaboration with the Associate Dean, Clinical Affairs, develops and implements guidelines and procedures for clinical charting, treatment reporting, clinical administration, patient financial management, and the interface with the AbelDent database. Undertakes ad hoc initiatives as required to support operational needs and ensure the smooth, efficient and effective functioning of the clinic. Other Qualifying Skills and/or Abilities: In-depth knowledge of and management experience in a dental clinical setting, hospital, or relevant healthcare environment is required. Experience working with clinical and administrative software systems is required. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills are required. Client-focused and service-oriented, with a demonstrated ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with individuals at all levels. Demonstrated ability to handle sensitive and complex situations effectively and diplomatically. Proven knowledge and experience in financial management and budget planning. Graduate degree in Business Administration, Finance, or a related field is an asset. Experience with McGill financial information systems is an asset.   As one of Montreal's Top Employers, here is what we offer: Competitive benefits package (Health, Dental, Life Insurance) Defined contribution pension plan (with employer contribution up to 10%) Group Registered Retirement Savings Plan (RRSP) and Tax Free Savings Account (TFSA) Competitive vacation policy Two (2) personal days Two (2) floating holidays Nine (9) \"Summer Fridays\" - paid days off between the St-Jean Baptiste holiday and Labour Day Paid time off over the December holiday period Tuition waiver for regular employees and their dependents Up to two (2) days of remote work per week where the position permits Before applying, please note that to work at McGill University, you must be both authorized to work in Canada and willing to work in the province of Quebec at the campus where the position is based / located. Knowledge of English: McGill University is an English-language university where day to day duties may require English communication both verbally and in writing. The level of English required for this position has been assessed at a level #4 on a scale of 0-4 . For a definition of our language proficiency levels, please click here . Minimum Education and Experience: Bachelor's Degree 3 Years Related Experience / Annual Salary: (MPEX Grade 04) $66,190.00 - $82,740.00 - $99,290.00 Job Profile: MPEX-ADM2A - General Administration - Professional 2 Hours per Week: 33.75 (Full time) Supervisor: Associate Director, Administration Position End Date (If applicable): 2027-10-30 Deadline to Apply: 2026-11-06 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Sherbrooke-680/Teaching-Assistant-RUSS-224---Winter-2027_JR0000082345": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant RUSS 224 - Winter 2027",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Department of Languages, Literatures and Cultures Course Title: Russian 19th Century: Literary Giants 2 Course Code: RUSS 224 001 Estimated Number of Positions: 1 Total Hours of Work per Term: 180 TA positions only available to McGill registered graduate students You must be a student registered at McGill University in an MA or PhD degree program in the Winter 2027 term. Hiring Unit: Department of Languages, Literatures and Cultures Course Title and Course Number: RUSS 224 Russian 19th Century: Literary Giants 2 Estimated Number of Positions: 1 position Total Hours of Work per Term: 180 hours * hours are dependent on course enrolment Job Description: Conference leader; assisting students (holding office hours, study groups). Maintaining Web CT material (scanning, uploading, research), including working with and learning from McGill ETG, as necessary. Other related activities. Qualifications: Must be a registered graduate student (M.A. or Ph.D.) in the Russian Studies Program, in the Department of Languages, Literatures, and Cultures at McGill University. Experience working with computers, internet, and scanners; must be comfortable in dealing with students as individuals or in a group. Excellent organization and communication skills. Required documentation: Please include a CV and Cover letter explaining why you are the best candidate. Hourly Salary: $38.46 Position Start Date: January 5, 2027 Position End Date: May 7, 2027   Deadline to Apply: October 29, 2026 International students must have a valid study permit, social Insurance number (SIN), and Canadian bank account. McGill University is an English-language University where most teaching and research activities are conducted in the English language, thereby requiring English communication both verbally and in writing. Hourly Salary: $38.46 Position Start Date: 2026-10-14 Position End Date: 2027-05-07 Deadline to Apply: 2026-10-29 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
