    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Strathcona-AnatDent/Teaching-Assistant--ANAT-314---Human-Musculoskeletal-Anatomy_JR0000082012": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant: ANAT 314 - Human Musculoskeletal Anatomy",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Anatomy & Cell Biology Course Title: Human Musculoskeletal Anatomy Course Code: ANAT 314 001 Estimated Number of Positions: 1 Total Hours of Work per Term: 55 Hiring Unit: Anatomy and Cell Biology Course Title and Course Number: ANAT 314 - Human Musculoskeletal Anatomy Estimated Number of Positions: 1 Total Hours of Work per Term: 55 Position Summary: TA should attend classes and provide weekly office hours to students. Prior to each lab session, TA will be responsible for fully familiarizing with the lab topics covering musculoskeletal anatomy. TA will be required to work with large volumes of students to illustrate clinical and laboratory anatomy at an undergraduate level. TA will assist in the labs, implementation and grading of exams and assignments. TA, in liaison with the course instructor, is required to coordinate and assign duties to Undergraduate course assistants (UCAs). TA will be responsible for supervising the lab set up, assisting UCAs with retrieving specimens to present to assigned student groups, and upon lab completion, with returning specimens to their assigned storage space and with lab clean-up. TA will also be responsible for supporting the UCA team during teaching activities using teaching models, prosections and other media; and to direct small teaching groups during the lab sessions. TA is responsible for reinforcing the laboratory rules and code of conduct in the lab, and to oversee all safety precautions regarding proper handling of specimens.  Qualifications: Demonstrated ability to teach human anatomy. Must have previously taken ANAT 214 and ANAT 314 (or equivalent). Extensive knowledge of the gross anatomy of the musculoskeletal system (bone, joints, muscles and neurovascular structures) of the head, neck, trunk, upper and lower limbs regions of the human body is required. Must be able to give in-depth lab demonstrations to students; emphasizes functional and clinical anatomy; must have a good understanding of surface anatomy; and know how to read medical imaging. Demonstrated leadership experience in supervising undergraduate students. Proven organizational skills with attention to detail and accuracy. Effective communication skills in English (spoken and written) are essential.  Hourly Salary: $38.46 Position Start Date: 2027-01-04 Position End Date: 2027-05-07 Deadline to Apply: 2026-11-02 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
    },
    "https://mcgill.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/mcgill_careers/job/Strathcona-AnatDent/Teaching-Assistant--ANAT-322---Neuroendocrinology_JR0000082025": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant: ANAT 322 - Neuroendocrinology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Anatomy & Cell Biology Course Title: Neuroendocrinology Course Code: ANAT 322 001 Estimated Number of Positions: 1 Total Hours of Work per Term: 80 Hiring Unit: Anatomy and Cell Biology Course Title and Course Number: ANAT 322 - Neuroendocrinology Estimated Number of Positions: 1 Total Hours of Work per Term: 80 Position Summary: TA must follow lectures with videorecordings and material supplied for live lectures. The TA also manages chat line to collect questions and comments from students. TA is responsible for monitoring the discussion board in MyCourses and answering questions about the course or referring to lecturers if necessary. TA manages online quizzes and exams or assignments. Serves as a link to course coordinator and instructors. Helps manage grading of exams if appropriate. Qualifications: Must have previously taken and passed ANAT322 or equivalent course. Demonstrated knowledge of the principles of Neuroendocrinology. Good organization and communication skills. Excellent skills with remote teaching and assessments. Prior Teaching Assistant experience is an asset. Effective communication skills in English are essential. Hourly Salary: $38.46 Position Start Date: 2027-01-04 Position End Date: 2027-05-07 Deadline to Apply: 2026-11-02 McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
