      "title": "Teaching Assistant DENT 245",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nPart time\n\nPlease refer to the  How to Apply for a Job (for External Candidates)   job aid for instructions on how to apply. If you are an active McGill employee (ie: currently in an active contract or position at McGill University), do not apply through this Career Site. Login to your McGill Workday account and apply to this posting using the Find Jobs report (type Find Jobs in the search bar). Hiring Unit: Course Title: Introduction to restorative dentistry Course Code: DENT 245 Estimated Number of Positions: 1 Total Hours of Work per Term: 130 Hiring Unit: Dental Medicine and Oral Health Sciences Course Title and Course Number: Restorative Dentistry DENT 245 Estimated Number of Positions: 1 Total Hours of Work per Term: 130 hours Job description:  Teaching and Mentorship - Teach, facilitate and mentor students in learning the basic procedures for fixed prosthodontics in a simulated setting. - Evaluate students’ assignments and provide feedback. - Demonstrate proper technical steps to individual students when required. - Supervise examination sessions.   Qualifications requises / Qualifications required:   - DMD from a Faculty of Dentistry. - Experience with teaching simulation training for pre-clinical dental students in fixed prosthodontics is considered an asset for this position.   Knowledge and experience with teaching fixed prosthodontic simulation procedures: Tooth preparation for crowns and bridges Temporary crown fabrication with PMMA and Composite Adjustments and cementation of crowns Knowledge on the use of digital scanners is an asset Name & Title of Course Supervisor: Dr. Samer Abi Nader, Associate Dean UGDE Hourly Salary: $38.46 Position Start Date: 2026-10-05 Position End Date: 2027-06-03 Deadline to Apply: McGill University hires on the basis of merit and is strongly committed to equity and diversity within its community. We welcome applications from racialized persons/visible minorities, women, Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and persons of minority sexual orientations and gender identities, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with diverse communities. McGill implements an employment equity program and encourages members of designated groups to self-identify. Persons with disabilities who anticipate needing accommodations for any part of the application process may contact, in confidence, accessibilityrequest.hr@mcgill.ca ."
